From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indiesaudi <16909576+indiesaudi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:30:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ir3/array_to_ssa: Resolve trivial phi chains in lookup_value

remove_trivial_phi() stores the replacement of a trivial phi in
phi->data. When that replacement is itself a phi that is found to be
trivial later, lookup_value() returned the intermediate phi, which
remove_trivial_phi() has already dropped from the block. Instructions
kept a reference to the removed phi, and the first pass to touch it
(ir3_dce, ir3_cse or register allocation) crashed reading freed IR,
failing vkCreateComputePipelines with an access violation.

Follow the data chain to the final definition. A non-trivial phi has
data pointing at its own destination, which ends the walk.

Source: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/issues/748#issuecomment-6373073950
carried by https://github.com/armada-os/armada/pull/829
The patched file is SPDX MIT, as is the patch.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
index dacd516..2858322 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
@@ -161,10 +161,12 @@ remove_trivial_phi(struct ir3_instruction *phi)
 static struct ir3_register *
 lookup_value(struct ir3_register *reg)
 {
-   if (!reg)
-      return NULL;
-   if (reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI)
-      return reg->instr->data;
+   while (reg && reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI) {
+      struct ir3_register *next = reg->instr->data;
+      if (next == reg)
+         break;
+      reg = next;
+   }
    return reg;
 }
 
